  "process_scope": "Listed build/query jobs terminal. Three REA captures terminal; owned groups cleanup within reported limits. Owned payload/GSI loop lookup empty and host selinuxfs lookup empty after final capture; no persistent target. Preboot handles historical.",
  "tests": [
    "Original Linux libselinux3.11 + same-version headers built without API/source patches. AOSP3.7 host full build fails in stale DB backend; preserve it, use proper upstream Linux component rather than patch individual backends. Android/Bionic library remains original and separate.",
    "Helper regular exec avoids non-async-safe library calls in Rust pre_exec. Fixed coordinator path, expected actor, kernel classes/mode, root-owned single-link0700 RO inode and original init_exec label checked before original setexeccon_raw/fexecve. No assignment attempted in unloaded policy negative tests.",
    "Worker normal mode now requires real u:r:init:s0 and classes, enforcing; explicit MAC integration diagnostic also permits permissive but still requires actual identity/classes. Legacy diagnostic remains explicitly non-MAC.",
    "32MiB ext4 payload,10 entries: original Linux loader/libs under /archtv/lib, Rust supervisor/helper under /archtv/bin, original-linked Bionic coordinator with Android PT_INTERP. Offline UID/GID/mode/xattr bytes, dumped content hashes and e2fsck0 checked. Not a mounted/assigned context proof.",
    "Actual REA three runs: first loader lacked execute bit (EACCES), second exposed exact-path Android namespace/ICU failure. Both retained. Corrected loader mode and mapped only trusted /archtv/bin to original system namespace, preserving original namespace bodies/APEX links. Linux config metadata private, not host /etc or fake kernel state.",
    "Final REA: normal helper78, integration helper78 at absent policy classes, worker MAC guard78/no startup. Diagnostic Rust direct-child Bionic startup\u2192observe\u2192STOP\u2192actual child0. Original GSI mounted RO, prepared APEX tree reused RO; diagnostic Android libselinux ignores RO selinuxfs by original design, not authorization success.",
    "Original policy three variants compile0 with neverallow enabled. Final selected queries 44 have expected0/7 outcomes, no errors. Read-only selinuxfs access for original host library added; write/admin and redundant check_context remain denied. No policy loaded; kernel enforcing0/policyload0."
  ],
